{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795248669,"nonce":"pRJbrarjZzeTBx2svMHmgBal/ZU=","title":"Concurrent Headless sessions in one process can lose the theme stylesheet","message":"Two `Headless` sessions on parallel `cargo test` threads, each installing the same `BlincTheme::bundle().with_css(..)`, intermittently render an element with none of its rules: no size, no border, no shadow. One session per process (nextest, as CI runs it) is stable. The theme state the stylesheet travels through is process-wide.\n\nSeen while writing `blinc_recorder/tests/box_shadow_inset.rs`, which keeps both of its cases in one test for this reason. Any multi-test file whose tests rely on theme CSS is exposed under plain `cargo test`.","files":null}]}